hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1041","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) made a vow to perform i'tikaf (seclusion) in the Mosque al-Haram during the period of ignorance. He asked the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ instructed him to fulfill his i'tikaf in Islam."
"1042","Urwah bin Udhaynah narrated that I set out (for Hajj) with my grandmother; she had vowed to walk to the House of Allah. But along the way, she became unable (to continue walking). So I asked Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) about the matter, and Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""Tell her to ride, then walk, and whenever she becomes unable, let her ride."" Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""And a sacrifice is obligatory upon her."
"1043","It is narrated from Tawus that the Prophet ﷺ passed by Abu Israil, who was standing in the sun. The Prophet ﷺ asked, ""What is the matter with him?"" The people said, ""He has vowed that he will not go into the shade, nor sit down, nor speak to anyone, and that he will fast."" So the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to seek shade, to sit down, and to speak to people, and to complete his fast, and he did not order him to offer any expiation."
"1044","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes a vow to obey Allah, let him obey Allah; and whoever makes a vow to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."
"1045","It is narrated from Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no (fulfillment of) vow in disobedience to Allah, nor is it necessary to fulfill a vow regarding that which the son of Adam does not possess."
"1046","It is narrated from Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible to fulfill a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor a vow regarding that which the son of Adam does not possess."
"1047","It is narrated from Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A woman from the Ansar was taken captive, while the she-camel (Adba) had been captured before her. Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Perhaps it was the Prophet’s ﷺ she-camel because the last part of the hadith indicates this. Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) said: That woman was among them (the disbelievers) and they would bring their camels to her. One night, the woman escaped from captivity and came to the camels. Whenever she approached a camel and touched it, it would make a sound, so she would leave it, until she came to that she-camel and touched it, and it did not make a sound. And it was a very strong she-camel. The woman sat on its back, then she urged it on and it set off. That night, they searched for her but could not overpower her. The woman made a vow that if Allah saved her by means of it, she would sacrifice it. When the woman reached Madinah, the people recognized the she-camel and said: This is the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The woman said that she had made a vow that if Allah saved her by means of it, she would slaughter it. Upon hearing this, the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: By Allah! Do not slaughter it until we seek permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They came to him ﷺ and told him the whole story, that such-and-such woman came on your she-camel and made a vow that if Allah saved her by means of it, she would slaughter it. Upon this, he ﷺ said (in amazement): “Subhan Allah! The woman has given a bad reward, that Allah saved her and she wants to slaughter it. There is no vow in that which involves disobedience to Allah or in that which a human or son of Adam does not own.”"
"1048","It is narrated from Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that a group attacked and took away a woman from the Ansar and the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The woman and the she-camel were with them, then the woman escaped and mounted the she-camel. She came to Madinah and the Prophet’s ﷺ she-camel was recognized. The woman said: I had vowed that if Allah saved me on its back, I would slaughter it. The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) stopped her from slaughtering it until she could mention this to the Prophet ﷺ. When she spoke to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “You have given it a bad reward, that Allah saved you on its back and you wish to slaughter it. There is no vow in disobedience to Allah or concerning what the son of Adam does not own.” Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sufyan and Abdul Wahhab both said together, or one of them said in the hadith, that the Prophet ﷺ took hold of his she-camel."
